;; stdlib/ecowar/town_cap_mod.prn — CAP, the real "capping a base" mod (EMILY/BACKLOG.md SECTION
;; 381). Founder real-time: "even the win con should be mods - capping a base should work as a mod
;; or a collection of mods and the wincon mod should interface with that mod via the ALLCAP mod or
;; something like that."
;;
;; Real, checked-first finding this design builds on: the actual DECISION of whether a capture
;; attempt succeeds was already mod-driven before this pass -- every real town type's own
;; convert-resistance function (ecowar/frontier_village_mod.prn's on-frontier-village-convert-
;; resistance, ecowar/walled_hamlet_mod.prn's on-walled-hamlet-convert-resistance) already decides
;; how hard a town is to flip. What was NOT a mod: the ANNOUNCEMENT that a capture actually
;; happened. This mod is that announcement, following the same "the mod is the trigger, host C
;; does the real work" shape every trigger-only mod in this repo already uses (bloodflower_mod.prn
;; is the closest real precedent -- it too is a bare dispatch into REFLUX plus one other real host
;; call). packages/livingmap/town.c's own town_attempt_convert calls on-town-captured directly
;; by name, exactly once, right after a real successful flip -- same call-by-name convention every
;; mod ABI in this repo already uses; REGISTRATION isn't real (VS0 has no function pointers), only
;; the shared REFLUX log genuinely decouples what happens AFTER this mod runs.
;;
;; ABI: on-town-captured is called from town_attempt_convert (packages/livingmap/town.c) the
;; instant conversion_progress crosses 100 -- the same real moment LIVING_MAP_EVENT_TOWN_CONVERTED
;; already fires. Dispatches REFLUX_ACTION_TOWN_CAPPED(town-id, old-faction, new-faction) via the
;; real reflux_dispatch FFI call (stdlib/reflux/reflux.prn, packages/reflux/reflux_runtime.c) --
;; same plain inline-c escape bloodflower_mod.prn's own on-moon-zenith already established for
;; calling into REFLUX. ecowar/allcap_mod.prn (a SEPARATE mod, this one never imports or calls it)
;; is the real, first subscriber -- see that file's own header comment.

(module ecowar/town-cap-mod)
(export on-town-captured)

(defn on-town-captured [(town-id : I32) (old-faction : I32) (new-faction : I32)] : Unit
  #target
  {:c (inline-c "reflux_dispatch(REFLUX_ACTION_TOWN_CAPPED, town_id, old_faction, new_faction);")})
